Question Title: Build Pipeline Directory Tree

Question Link: https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/r2ui5gw5lhqt?lecture_hash=n9ynhcuvkld8


Solution:
mkdir -p pipeline/stages/build
mkdir -p pipeline/stages/test/unit/integration
mkdir -p pipeline/env/staging
mkdir -p pipeline/env/prod
mkdir -p pipeline/artifacts/old

chmod 750 pipeline/stages
chmod 770 pipeline/artifacts
chmod 700 pipeline/env

touch pipeline/stages/build/app.py pipeline/stages/build/config.json pipeline/stages/build/NOTES.md
echo "Build stage initialized." > pipeline/stages/build/NOTES.md

touch pipeline/artifacts/old/build.log pipeline/artifacts/old/test.log pipeline/artifacts/old/deploy.log
chmod 640 pipeline/artifacts/old/build.log pipeline/artifacts/old/test.log pipeline/artifacts/old/deploy.log

Approach:
1. Created the whole directory tree with mkdir -p, which also creates missing parent folders.
2. Set permissions on stages (750), artifacts (770) and env (700) using the numeric form, where read = 4, write = 2, execute = 1.
3. Created the three empty files in stages/build with touch and wrote the single line into NOTES.md with echo.
4. Created the three log files in artifacts/old and set them to 640, so the owner can read and write, the group can only read, and others have no access.